// The owner's verdict on v2 (2026-11-19): at most 70 s; the desert first, under "21 WORLDS"; no hay bales, no Dream; the big top
// before the hand-over, which leads straight into the shooting; the player's own view and precise aim; the laser net and its
// projectors before the first game; every trailer shot moving (a still lens only in the player's view, with the HUD); the new saucer;
// the grid without a turning cycle; his favourite scenes first; desert-style music for the slow part; a friendly "still in
// development" at the end with the address set lower; and a last shot of one game while every world swaps behind it.
// Every play "in" was found at 60 frames a second (the size does not matter, the rate does). Camera paths count from a clip's
// window start, a quarter second before its "in" (Tools/trailer/paths).
